# Nougat extraction stub — s100-099-entwined-nhej-mechanistic

**Status:** NOT RUN.

## Reason
Existing OCR pipeline for this slot used `pdftotext -layout` (see
`ocr/raw_layout.txt`, `ocr/supp_layout.txt`) plus 300 dpi PNG
rendering of Supplementary Figures S8-S11 for the rate-constant
schematic labels. Backfill rule: preserve existing artifacts; do
not re-run sims/extractions. This stub exists so that the standard
8-artifact directory shape is populated.

## If Nougat is later run
- Suggested target: nougat 0.1.0-small on `source/paper.pdf` and
  `source/supplementary.pdf`
- Suggested endpoint: uicgpu A100 (free) for the mmd inference
- Suggested output: `extraction/paper.nougat.mmd`,
  `extraction/supplementary.nougat.mmd`

## Known limits for THIS paper
- Figures S8-S11 embed the per-scenario rate constants as vector
  text inside schematic boxes/arrows. Nougat inherits mathpix-style
  block detection; vector-text-inside-figure labels historically
  survive better than in pdftotext but still degrade at native
  resolution. Even a successful Nougat pass may not close blocker
  (b) (need machine-readable rate-constant table).
- The main paper text was already extractable via pdftotext, so
  Nougat would primarily buy formula/equation fidelity for the
  Methods section (bimolecular synapsis kinetics) rather than new
  scientific content.

Paper title: Mechanistic modelling supports entwined rather than
exclusively competitive DNA double-strand break repair pathway.
DOI: 10.1038/s41598-019-42901-8.
